course: dictionary
lesson: 4292
title: One word, many greys
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Grey» is a small word with several jobs. It can be a colour, as in «grey skies». It can describe things (an adjective), name the colour itself (a noun), or act as a verb, as in «go grey», meaning to turn grey. The words around it tell you which meaning is in use.
explain: Look at «Everyone gets older: grey hair, glasses and stiffer knees come.» The clue is older: grey hair is the white or silver hair that comes with age. Ask yourself what the sentence says about the people, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
explain: «A grey area» is different again. It is not about a colour at all. It means something that is not clearly right or wrong, so when you see area next to grey, do not picture a patch of colour.
fact: Grey is a colour between black and white, like clouds before rain, ash or an elephant.
fact: «Grey hair» is the white or silver hair of older people.
fact: «A grey day» is dull and cloudy.
fact: «Grey» can be an adjective (greyer, greyest), a noun, or a verb, as in «go grey». US spelling is gray.
fact: «A grey area» means something not clearly right or wrong.
exercise: «The sky went grey before the storm.» What does grey mean here? | Cold and sharp to touch | *A dull colour between black and white | Covered in green leaves | A bright gold colour
exercise: «Grandpa's grey hair shone in the sunshine.» What does grey hair mean? | Hair dyed bright red | *White or silver hair that comes with age | Hair cut very short | Hair full of dust
exercise: «The rule is a grey area, so nobody is sure if it is allowed.» What does grey area mean? | A patch of dirty ground | A colour between red and blue | A place where the sun never shines | *Something not clearly right or wrong
test: Which phrase uses grey as a verb? | grey day | grey area | grey squirrel | *go grey
test: In «Everyone gets older: grey hair, glasses and stiffer knees come», which word is the clue to the meaning of grey hair? | come | *older | knees | glasses
exam: In «The Rat walks ahead, his eyes fixed on the straight grey road», which meaning of grey fits? | *A colour between black and white | To turn grey | Not clearly right or wrong | White hair of older people
